# trivy CVE waivers
#
# One CVE per line. Every entry MUST have a comment on the line above
# explaining:
#   1. Why the CVE does not apply (or risk is acceptable)
#   2. Who waived it and when
#   3. When to revisit (date or "next image base bump")
#
# Example:
#   # 2026-05-22 / @don-jose-dev / chromium pulls libxml2 transitively but we
#   # never parse untrusted XML; revisit on next base image bump.
#   CVE-2026-12345
#
# Empty waiver list is the desired steady state — every CVE here is technical
# debt. Prefer base image bumps over waivers.
